OOPS CONCEPT:
¾ Object Oriented Programing Structure
¾ OOPS is a method of implementation in which programs are organized as collection of objects, class
and methods

Page 5
Oops principles are
1. Class
2. Method
3. Object
4. Abstraction
5. Encapsulation
6. Inheritance
7. Polymorphism
CLASS:
¾ Class is nothing but collection of methods or collection of objects.
x Project name : Should be in Pascal notation
x Pascal notation : Each word of the first letter should be in capital
x src - Source file
x Class name: Pascal notation
x Package creation: ex, org.cts.scope-All small letters
Syntax:
(First type class name and click ctrl +space)
public class Bank {
} // Bank is a class name
Public-Access specifier
METHOD:
¾ Set of action to be performed
Method name: camel notation
Camel notation: First word should be small after every word of the first letter should be capital
Syntax:
public void dummy() {
// Here dummy is a method name
 }
Main Method:
public static void main(String[] args) {
}
Main methodÆ type main and click ctrl +space

Page 6
OBJECT:
¾ Run time memory allocation
¾ Using object we call the any methods
Syntax:
(Class name) (Object name) =new (Class name) ();
¾ AlignmentÆ ctrl + shift+ F
¾ Run Æ ctrl +F11
Example program:
1. StudentDatabase
public class StudentInfo {
public void Studentname() {
System.out.println("Name:Vengat");
}
public void studentList() {
System.out.println();
}
public void StudentMark() {
System.out.println("Mark:1005");
}
public void StudentAddress() {
System.out.println("Address: Chennai");
}
public static void main(String[] arg) {
StudentInfo info = new StudentInfo();
info.Studentname();
info.StudentMark();
info.StudentAddress();
}
}
2.ECommerce
